  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1111 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nSome subtle height rises occur over the region as the ridge over\nthe Southwest expands some. Our area will be under its influence\non its eastern side into early next week. Expect a multi-day\nstretch of hot (triple digit heat eastern OK) and dry weather.\nHeat headlines are likely to continue daily during this time. It\nis not unusual for it to be hot this time of year. The period from\nmid-July to mid-August is the hottest period of the year\nclimatologically.\n\nRain/storm chances increase some for the latter half of the week\nas the ridge over the Southwest goes away and reforms over the\nGulf Coast/Southeast. A weak boundary may try to push into the\nregion from the north/northeast and focus activity. Forecast highs\nalso trend relatively cooler during this time as well.\n\nLacy",
